      "data": {
        "body": "Implement the new interface model without breaking the existing graph library: Ports receive, Handles specialize Ports and act, Title-centered circular geometry projects endpoints, and legacy contracts compile into the normalized runtime representation.",
        "priority": "critical",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "Michael",
        "targetDate": "",
        "successMetrics": [
          "Legacy graphs retain their current rendering, navigation, and connection behavior.",
          "New graphs author Port and Handle primitives structurally without synthetic side handles.",
          "Circular interface geometry protects endpoint directions while interior content remains auto-arrangeable.",
          "The Dynamic Port Expansion smoke test passes.",
          "The repository root graph is migrated as the first native v2 graph."
        ],
