        "title": "Define the Port endpoint and behavior contract",
        "body": "Keep Port as the single authored endpoint primitive. Define independent acceptance and initiating behaviors, the drag result containing source and target identities or graph coordinates, and the rule that a handle is only the projected affordance of an actionable Port. Keep relationship meaning on edges and edge classes.",
        "priority": "critical",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Port declarations and their behaviors are inspectable graph artifacts.",
          "A Port with initiating behavior projects a handle affordance without creating a second endpoint primitive.",
          "Empty-drop behavior is explicit and optional.",
          "Surface exposure and portal consumption remain separate concerns."
        ],
