      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "body": "In edit mode, should the graph project a zoom-1 outline of the instantiated node behind its authored structure, replacing the ordinary Twilite logo? How should the Declaration-to-Title relationship establish root orientation and expected Port behavior without being mistaken for the rendered node's literal size?",
        "status": "answered",
        "owner": "",
        "resolutionPath": "In edit mode, resolve an explicit structural interface-title relationship between Declaration and Title. Center the projected frame on Title, derive its zoom-1 width and height from the Declaration's default exposed surface node, and use the Title-to-Declaration vector only for root orientation. Render the outline behind the graph in place of the watermark and hide it in Browse mode. Graphs without the explicit relationship retain legacy watermark behavior. The Graph Lab proof is github://mikemartinez1974/public/graphs/interface-frame-smoke.node.",
        "prominence": "medium",
        "definitionKey": "open-question",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "open-question",
